jobs.description:
Are you an experienced forklift operator who feels right at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to work for a stable company where you’ll work alongside a small, close-knit team to ensure everything runs smoothly? Then we have a great opportunity for you!

For a client in Weert, we’re looking for an experienced forklift operator who enjoys working a two-shift schedule. You’ll be joining a large logistics company where safety, teamwork, and a pleasant work atmosphere are key priorities.

What will you be doing?

As a forklift operator, you’ll be responsible for moving goods efficiently and safely within the warehouse. You’ll spend most of your workday operating the forklift. Together with four colleagues, you’ll ensure that all pallets and goods are placed in the correct locations and that outgoing orders are ready on time.

Your duties will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Scanning goods;
- Moving pallets and goods within the warehouse;
- Preparing outgoing orders for transport.

You’ll be operating a forklift with double forks, loading from the side. Do you have experience with this? If so, be sure to read on!

You’ve already gained considerable experience operating a forklift and understand how important it is to work safely and accurately. You’re flexible, keep a cool head during busy periods, and are comfortable working two different shifts.

In addition:

- You have recent experience as a forklift operator;
- You hold a valid forklift operator’s certificate;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You are available full-time;
- You work with precision and always put safety first.

Are you a hands-on worker, do you like working in an organized way, and do you feel at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to be part of one of Europe’s largest producers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position at our client in Waalwijk is perfect for you!

As a Logistics Employee, you play an important role in the logistics process surrounding the production of high-quality, custom-made sandwich panels for, among others, the bodywork industry and the defense sector. You ensure that materials, raw materials, and finished products are available at the right place and at the right time.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, in a close-knit team of colleagues. Order, overview, and safety are central to your daily tasks.

As a Logistics Employee, your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading goods using a forklift;

- Receiving and assisting drivers (first point of contact);

- Packing and preparing finished products for shipment;

- Managing internal logistics between the warehouse and production departments;

- Supplying raw materials to various production departments;

- Cleaning and organizing the warehouse and production halls;

- Ensuring a safe and tidy workplace.

Requirements

- You work in a structured manner and have an eye for order and safety;

- You hold a valid forklift certificate;

- You are a true team player;

- You have a good command of the Dutch or English language.

Looking for a job with fixed hours and want to work with a big logistics company? Look no further and apply now! You'll be working in a large warehouse in Wijchen, part of an international logistics organisation. From four warehouses on the same site, large volumes of goods go out every day to customers across Europe and beyond. Your work keeps that moving. You operate the EPT and make sure pallets get to the right place. You do that independently and accurately. When things get busy somewhere, you pitch in on another task. Nothing complicated, just doing your job well.

 - Proven, recent hands-on experience operating an EPT;
 - Available in dayshift Monday to Friday, 40 hours per week;
 - You speak and understand Dutch or English.

In a modern 13,500 m² warehouse, millions of order lines are processed each year. As an Order Picker using an Order Pick Truck (OPT), you play a key role in ensuring customer orders are collected accurately and on time. If you enjoy working actively in a fast-paced logistics environment, this could be the right opportunity for you.
Acerca de la empresaThis international B2B specialist in mobility accessories is a leading player in the Benelux with strong international ambitions. From a highly automated distribution center, over two million order lines are processed annually. The warehouse features an advanced OSR shuttle system, modern internal transport equipment, and dedicated ADR compartments for hazardous goods storage. Efficiency, safety, and quality are central within the logistics team.
Sobre el trabajoAs an Order Picker, you work independently within the picking aisles using an Order Pick Truck (OPT). You collect orders according to the Warehouse Management System (WMS) and check items for correct quantities and quality. Once completed, you prepare orders for shipment to ensure customers receive their products on time.
 You are also responsible for replenishing pick locations using internal transport equipment and identifying stock discrepancies. Maintaining a clean and safe work environment is essential, and you report any unsafe situations when necessary. You may also assist with loading activities when required. This is a full-time role in a 2-shift system with the following times:
 6:00 - 15:00 & 15:00 - 0:00.
Requisitos - MBO-level working and thinking ability;
 - Experience with an OPT, EPT, or similar internal transport equipment is a plus;
 - Physically fit and comfortable with active work;
 - Good command of the English language;
 - Accuracy and attention to detail;
 - Ability to handle workload and work under pressure;
 - Able to work independently and as part of a team;
 - Strong focus on working safely.
 - EU nationality.

